    "answer": "That's not in the record. Nothing in what I have describes a 'flapping' symptom or names the scout specifically in that context. The closest documented case is a persona-gate review: a synthetic panel of personas called a UI DONE at a healthy pace, but the next morning a real phone, in the real flow, called the result 'pretty much unusable' — catching browser chrome eating space and a modal reopening on every task switch. So there is a real-device check before calling things done, but not the flapping behavior you're asking about.",
